---
/**
 * About, in the Director's Cut language.
 *
 * Carries the Annual Report's letter (the piece with the most voice in it),
 * the interview answers that are about the person rather than a project, the
 * capabilities, and the full record of engagements.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Cut from '../layouts/Cut.astro';
import CutIcon from '../components/CutIcon.astro';
import { log, contact, tools, skillGroups, certs, recognition, hobbies, nowItems, podcasts } from '../lib/variants';
import { interview } from '../lib/interview';

import heroPortrait from '../assets/sayantan.jpg';
import sidePortrait from '../assets/sayantan-studio.jpg';

const capabilities = [
  { k: 'Product design', v: 'End to end, discovery through delivery. Flows, journeys, prototypes, interaction detail.' },
  { k: 'UX strategy', v: 'Turning a vague request into something a small team can build inside a quarter.' },
  { k: 'Design systems', v: 'Component libraries, tokens, and a written accessibility baseline. One system held across three products at Ericsson.' },
  { k: 'Research', v: 'Domain immersion, interviews, synthesis, usability testing, heuristic evaluation.' },
  { k: 'Design operations', v: 'File architecture, shared templates, and a research-to-design handoff a team of twenty actually used.' },
  { k: 'Accessibility', v: 'WCAG AA as a starting constraint rather than a pass at the end.' },
  { k: 'Stakeholder facilitation', v: 'Getting a product owner and a tech lead to a shared view of what a release can hold. At Ericsson that mattered more than any single screen.' },
  { k: 'Zero to one', v: 'Founding designer three times over. Taking a product from no design function at all to a shipped, documented system.' },
];

/** The answers that are about how I work rather than about one project. */
const DUPLICATES_THE_LETTER = 'What kind of designer are you, in one answer?';
const personal = interview.filter(
  (qa) => qa.a.trim().length > 0 && !qa.link && qa.q !== DUPLICATES_THE_LETTER
);
---

<Cut
  title="About, Sayantan Dutta"
  description="Product designer for enterprise SaaS and AI, based in Southampton. Five years across industrial safety, API infrastructure, design operations and a voice-first AI companion."
  navTone="dark"
  active="about"
>

<!-- Keeps the `pagehead` class: the layout's nav script measures whichever
     dark block opens the page by it, and the page's type and focus rings hang
     off it too. `ph-full` is what turns it into the home page's full frame. -->
<header class="pagehead ph-full">
  <figure class="ah-bg" aria-hidden="true">
    <Image src={heroPortrait} alt="" widths={[900, 1600]} sizes="100vw" loading="eager" />
  </figure>

  <div class="pagehead-in ah-in">
    <div class="at-copy">
      <p class="sec-k">About</p>
      <h1>I work best where complexity meets clarity, making difficult systems seamless.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Five years across industrial safety, enterprise SaaS, design operations and
        AI. Founding designer three times over. Based in {contact.base}, working
        with distributed teams since 2020.
      </p>
      <!-- Three ways out, one of them primary. Email is the ask; LinkedIn and
           the CV are both "check me" routes, so they read as a matched pair
           beside it rather than competing with it. -->
      <div class="at-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-on-dark" href={`mailto:${contact.email}`} data-ab="about:email"><CutIcon name="mail" />Get in touch</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost-dark" href={contact.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="me noopener" data-ab="about:linkedin"><CutIcon name="linkedin" />LinkedIn</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost-dark" href={contact.resume} data-ab="about:cv"><CutIcon name="download" />CV (PDF)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="main">

  <!-- ═══ THE LETTER ════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="band-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="sec-k">In my own words</p>
      <h2>Why this work, and not the other kind</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        The short version of how five years in enterprise and industrial
        software changed what I think good design is for.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="letter-grid">
    <div class="letter" data-reveal>
      <p>
        Most of what I have worked on, people did not choose. A safety engineer
        running a hazard study, a developer wiring up an API, a woman of
        seventy-five checking whether she has taken her tablets. None of them
        picked the software. It arrived with the job, or with the diagnosis.
      </p>
      <p>
        That changes what good means. Delight is not the measure. The measure is
        whether someone can get through the task on a bad day, at speed, while
        worried, without the interface adding to the problem. It is quieter work
        than consumer design and it takes longer to learn, because you cannot
        design the thing until you understand the job, and the job is usually
        more complicated than the brief admits.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over five years that has taken me from a three-year engagement on
        Ericsson’s API vertical, where I grew from product designer to design
        lead, to being the only designer in a room of three at dAIs Genie. The
        large team taught me that most of a design system is negotiation. The
        small one taught me that if you do not write it down, it does not exist.
      </p>
      <p class="sign">Sayantan Dutta</p>
      <p class="sign-role">Product designer · {contact.base}</p>
    </div>

    <aside class="letter-side" data-reveal style="--d:110ms">
      <figure class="ls-photo">
        <Image src={sidePortrait} alt="Sayantan Dutta" widths={[480, 860]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 70vw, 320px" />
      </figure>
      <dl class="ls-facts">
        <div><dt>Based</dt><dd>{contact.base}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Now</dt><dd>Founding product designer, dAIs Genie</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Education</dt><dd>MA Design Management, University of Southampton</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Working remotely since</dt><dd>2020</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ Q&A ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  {personal.length > 0 && (
    <section class="band band-talk">
      <div class="band-head" data-reveal>
        <p class="sec-k">In conversation</p>
        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <p class="sec-lede">
          The questions that usually come up once the portfolio is out of the way.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="qa">
        {personal.map((qa, i) => (
          <li data-reveal style={`--d:${Math.min(i, 3) * 60}ms`}>
            <p class="q-n" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
            <h3 class="q">{qa.q}</h3>
            <p class="a">{qa.a}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>
  )}

  <!-- ═══ CAPABILITIES ══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="band-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="sec-k">Capabilities</p>
      <h2>What I actually do</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        Six things, each one something I have been accountable for on a shipped
        product rather than a line on a skills list.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="caps" data-reveal>
      {capabilities.map((c) => <div><dt>{c.k}</dt><dd>{c.v}</dd></div>)}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ TOOLS AND SKILLS ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="band-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="sec-k">Tools and skills</p>
      <h2>What I work with</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        The stack I am fluent in, and the practices underneath it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- `role="list"` because the reset strips the bullets, and Safari drops
         list semantics with them. The marks are decorative; the name is the
         accessible content. -->
    <ul class="tool-grid" role="list" aria-label="Tools I work with" data-reveal>
      {tools.map((t) => (
        <li class="tool-tile">
          <img src={`/images/tools/${t.file}`} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" />
          <span>{t.name}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="skill-stack" data-reveal style="--d:90ms">
      {skillGroups.map((g) => (
        <div class="skill-row">
          <p class="skill-row-lbl">{g.label}</p>
          <ul class="skill-chips" role="list">
            {g.items.map((sk) => <li>{sk}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ RECORD ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="band-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="sec-k">Record</p>
      <h2>Where I have been</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        Every role in order, with the basis each one ran on.
      </p>
    </div>
    <!-- A real table all the way down. It used to restyle `tr` to a grid at
         phone widths, which drops the row and cell roles and leaves four
         unlabelled values in a column; a data table is exempt from 1.4.10
         reflow, so scrolling it inside a focusable labelled region keeps the
         headers attached and stays keyboard reachable. -->
    <div class="tbl-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Career record" data-reveal>
    <table class="record">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Period</th><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Company</th><th scope="col">Basis</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {log.slice().reverse().map((l) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="rc-when">{l.stamp}</td>
            <td class="rc-role">{l.role}</td>
            <td class="rc-org">{l.org}</td>
            <td class="rc-kind">{l.kind}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ CERTIFICATIONS AND RECOGNITION ════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="band-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="sec-k">Certifications and recognition</p>
      <h2>On the record elsewhere</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        The programmes I have finished, what I was given for the work, and
        where I show up outside a job.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="cert-grid" role="list" data-reveal>
      {certs.map((c) => (
        <li class="cert-card">
          <img src={`/images/certs/${c.logo}`} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="26" height="26" loading="lazy" />
          <p class="cert-title">{c.title}</p>
          <p class="cert-issuer">{c.issuer}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="skill-stack" data-reveal style="--d:90ms">
      {recognition.map((g) => (
        <div class="skill-row">
          <p class="skill-row-lbl">{g.label}</p>
          <ul class="skill-chips" role="list">
            {g.items.map((i) => (
              <li>
                {i.url
                  ? <a class="chip-link" href={i.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{i.name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                  : i.name}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ OUTSIDE OF WORK ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="band-head" data-reveal>
      <p class="sec-k">Outside of work</p>
      <h2>The rest of it</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        A curious person, happiest in the mountains, on a beach, or wandering
        somewhere new. Recently started learning the basics of German. Always
        looking for a good mocha, never the flat white.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="hobby-grid" role="list" aria-label="Interests" data-reveal>
      {hobbies.map((h) => (
        <li class="hobby-tile">
          <CutIcon name={h.icon} cls="hb-mark" />
          <span>{h.name}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <ul class="now-grid" role="list" data-reveal style="--d:90ms">
      {nowItems.map((n) => (
        <li class="now-card">
          <span class="now-mark" aria-hidden="true"><CutIcon name={n.icon} cls="hb-mark" /></span>
          <div>
            <p class="now-cat">{n.cat}</p>
            <p class="now-title">{n.title}</p>
            <p class="now-sub">{n.sub}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="pods" data-reveal style="--d:140ms">
      <p class="skill-row-lbl">Podcasts in rotation</p>
      <ul class="pod-list" role="list">
        {podcasts.map((pod) => (
          <li>
            <a href={pod.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <CutIcon name="mic" cls="hb-mark pod-mark" />
              {pod.name}
              <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ CLOSE ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="band about-end">
    <div class="ae-copy" data-reveal>
      <h2>Working on something people have to use?</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">That is the work I am best at. Tell me what you are weighing up.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ae-side" data-reveal style="--d:110ms">
      <p class="ae-k">Email</p>
      <p class="ae-mail"><a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`} data-ab="about-end:email">{contact.email}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<style>
  /* ── the masthead, built as the home page's hero ──
     Full frame, photograph behind, copy and buttons sitting on the floor of
     it. The scrim is the home page's, so the two pages open the same way. */
  .pagehead.ph-full {
    position: relative; overflow: hidden;
    min-height: 100svh; display: flex; align-items: flex-end;
    padding: clamp(3rem, 10vw, 7rem) var(--pad) clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }
  .ah-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 0; }
  .ah-bg img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 58% 28%; animation: push 26s ease-out forwards; }
  /* A tall frame crops a landscape source hard, which drops the face right
     behind the headline. Lift it so the copy lands on the shoulders. */
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .ah-bg img { object-position: 56% 13%; } }
  @keyframes push { from { transform: scale(1.1); } to { transform: none; } }
  .pagehead.ph-full::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1; pointer-events: none;
    background:
      linear-gradient(to top, var(--black) 4%, rgba(10,10,10,.88) 32%, rgba(10,10,10,.42) 68%, rgba(10,10,10,.6) 100%),
      linear-gradient(to right, var(--black) 0%, rgba(10,10,10,.56) 46%, transparent 78%);
  }
  /* A phone crops the photograph tight and pushes the lede onto a brighter
     part of it: #a3a3a0 measured 3.3:1 there against 7.2:1 at desktop. The
     horizontal wash does nothing in a narrow frame, so below 560 it gives
     way to a heavier vertical one. */
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .pagehead.ph-full::after {
      background: linear-gradient(to top, var(--black) 8%, rgba(10,10,10,.94) 52%, rgba(10,10,10,.5) 100%);
    }
  }
  .ah-in { position: relative; z-index: 2; width: 100%; }
  /* 14.5em, not the container: left to the full width this breaks into two
     lines, the second 1007px against a 625px lede under it, which is the
     same hanging shape the home page had. Three lines of 690, 508 and 651
     sit with the lede instead. `em` so the count holds as the type scales. */
  .at-copy h1 { margin: .9rem 0 0; max-width: 14.5em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .at-cta {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .7rem;
    margin-top: 2.2rem; padding-top: 1.8rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(244,244,243,.18); max-width: 52rem;
  }

  /* Same opening as the home page, in reading order. */
  @keyframes rise { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(18px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
  :global(html.anim) .at-copy .sec-k { animation: rise .7s var(--ease) both .06s; }
  :global(html.anim) .at-copy h1 { animation: rise .85s var(--ease) both .18s; }
  :global(html.anim) .at-copy .lead { animation: rise .7s var(--ease) both .4s; }
  :global(html.anim) .at-cta { animation: rise .7s var(--ease) both .52s; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .ah-bg img { animation: none; transform: none; } }

  /* ── the letter ── */
  .letter-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 320px); gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .letter-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .letter-side { max-width: 380px; } }
  .letter { max-width: 62ch; }
  .letter p { font-family: var(--read); font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.08rem); color: var(--ink-2); }
  .letter p + p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .letter p:first-child::first-letter {
    float: left; font-family: var(--read); font-size: 3.4em; line-height: .84;
    padding: .06em .09em 0 0; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600;
  }
  .sign { margin-top: 2rem !important; font-family: var(--display) !important; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--ink) !important; }
  .sign-role { margin-top: .1rem !important; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--faint) !important; font-family: var(--display) !important; }

  .letter-side { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 1.5rem); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .letter-side { position: static; } }
  .ls-photo img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; object-fit: cover; object-position: center 15%; border-radius: 4px; }
  .ls-facts { margin-top: 1.6rem; display: grid; gap: 1rem; padding-top: 1.4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .ls-facts dt { font-size: var(--micro); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); }
  .ls-facts dd { font-size: .9rem; margin-top: .15rem; }

  /* ── capabilities ── */
  .caps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: var(--line); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .caps > div { background: var(--paper); padding: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.6rem); transition: background var(--quick) var(--ease); }
  .caps > div:hover { background: #fff; }
  .caps dt { font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: .35rem; }
  .caps dd { font-family: var(--read); color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .95rem; }
  /* ── tools and skills ──
     The main site's grid, rebuilt on paper. The logos ship with their own
     brand colour, so they sit grey until a tile is hovered and only then
     come up in full, which keeps fourteen marks from shouting at once. */
  .tool-grid {
    /* 140px floor puts exactly seven across the band, so fourteen tools make
       two full rows rather than a thin strip with a short tail. */
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(140px, 1fr));
    gap: .6rem; margin-bottom: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
  }
  /* At 320 the band is 282px, two tiles at the 140 floor need 290, and the
     grid falls to a single column fourteen rows deep. Drop the floor just
     for the narrowest phones so it stays two across. */
  @media (max-width: 360px) {
    .tool-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(104px, 1fr)); }
  }
  .tool-tile {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .6rem;
    padding: 1.4rem .5rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    transition: border-color var(--quick) var(--ease), background var(--quick) var(--ease), transform var(--quick) var(--ease);
  }
  .tool-tile img {
    width: 28px; height: 28px; object-fit: contain;
    filter: grayscale(1) opacity(.5);
    transition: filter var(--quick) var(--ease), transform var(--quick) var(--ease);
  }
  .tool-tile span {
    font-size: var(--micro); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faint); text-align: center; transition: color var(--quick) var(--ease);
  }
  .tool-tile:hover { border-color: var(--edge); background: #fff; transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .tool-tile:hover img { filter: none; transform: scale(1.06); }
  .tool-tile:hover span { color: var(--ink); }

  .skill-stack { display: grid; gap: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); }
  .skill-row-lbl { font-size: var(--micro); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); margin-bottom: .7rem; }
  .skill-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .45rem; }
  .skill-chips li {
    font-size: .82rem; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--ink-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 2px; padding: .5rem .75rem; background: var(--paper-2);
    transition: border-color var(--quick) var(--ease), color var(--quick) var(--ease), background var(--quick) var(--ease);
  }
  .skill-chips li:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--ink); background: #fff; }

  /* ── certifications ── */
  .cert-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: .6rem; margin-bottom: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
  }
  .cert-card {
    padding: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--paper-2); transition: background var(--quick) var(--ease), border-color var(--quick) var(--ease);
  }
  .cert-card:hover { background: #fff; border-color: var(--edge); }
  .cert-card img { width: 26px; height: 26px; object-fit: contain; margin-bottom: .9rem; filter: grayscale(1) opacity(.55); transition: filter var(--quick) var(--ease); }
  .cert-card:hover img { filter: none; }
  .cert-title { font-weight: 700; font-size: .98rem; }
  .cert-issuer { margin-top: .25rem; font-size: var(--micro); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); }

  /* ── outside of work ── */
  .hobby-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(140px, 1fr));
    gap: .6rem; margin-bottom: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
  }
  /* Eight tiles want four and four, not seven and a straggler, so the column
     count is fixed once there is room for it rather than left to auto-fill. */
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .hobby-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 360px) { .hobby-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(104px, 1fr)); } }
  .hobby-tile {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .6rem;
    padding: 1.4rem .5rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 2px; background: var(--paper-2);
    transition: border-color var(--quick) var(--ease), background var(--quick) var(--ease), transform var(--quick) var(--ease);
  }
  .hobby-tile:hover { border-color: var(--edge); background: #fff; transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .hobby-tile span { font-size: var(--micro); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); text-align: center; }
  .hobby-tile:hover span { color: var(--ink); }
  :global(.hb-mark) { width: 22px; height: 22px; color: var(--ink-2); }

  .now-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: .6rem; margin-bottom: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
  }
  .now-card {
    display: flex; gap: .9rem; align-items: flex-start;
    padding: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 2px; background: var(--paper-2);
  }
  .now-mark { display: grid; place-items: center; flex: 0 0 auto; width: 38px; height: 38px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--paper); }
  .now-cat { font-size: var(--micro); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); }
  .now-title { font-family: var(--read); font-size: 1.08rem; margin-top: .3rem; }
  .now-sub { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin-top: .25rem; }

  .pod-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .45rem; }
  /* A chip that is a link has to clear the 44px target floor the static
     skill chips do not, so it carries its own padding rather than the
     chip's. Shared by the community row and the podcasts. */
  .chip-link, .pod-list a {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .45rem; min-height: 44px;
    font-size: .82rem; color: var(--ink-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 2px; padding: .4rem .75rem; background: var(--paper-2);
    transition: border-color var(--quick) var(--ease), color var(--quick) var(--ease), background var(--quick) var(--ease);
  }
  .chip-link:hover, .pod-list a:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--ink); background: #fff; }
  :global(.pod-mark) { width: 15px; height: 15px; color: var(--accent); }
  .chip-link > span, .pod-list a > span { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--faint); }
  /* The row mixes linked and plain chips, so the plain ones drop their own
     box when a link is inside and the two line up on one baseline. */
  .skill-chips li:has(.chip-link) { padding: 0; border: 0; background: none; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .tool-tile:hover, .hobby-tile:hover { transform: none; }
    .tool-tile:hover img { transform: none; }
  }

  /* ── close ── */
  .about-end {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 22rem);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem); align-items: end;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .about-end { grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; } }
  .about-end h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); max-width: 20ch; }
  .about-end .sec-lede { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .ae-side { padding-top: 1.4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .ae-k { font-size: var(--micro); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); }
  .ae-mail { margin-top: .6rem; font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.4vw, 1.5rem); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.03em; word-break: break-word; }
  .ae-mail a { display: inline-block; padding-block: .35rem; border-bottom: 2.5px solid var(--accent); transition: color var(--quick) var(--ease); }
  .ae-mail a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
